We investigate the bistar-shaped ground state solution for the given biharmonic Choquard type equation \begin{align*}
  \begin{split}
  \Delta^2u-Lu=p(|x|e^{-|x|^2})u+\lambda u+\beta u^3,
  \end{split}
  \end{align*} under the constraints $u\in H^4_{\text{rad}}(\mathbb{R}^4)$ and $u\neq 0$. The parameters in the equation are $\beta$, $\lambda$ and $p$, which vary with $u$. Utilizing the variational method, we establish a continuous variationally critical value for the problem and then leverage a novel standardization technique to demonstrate the existence of bistar-shaped ground state solutions for an appropriately chosen parameter $p$. Additionally, we show that these solutions standardize the critical value under certain conditions.

The analysis of time-critical data, particularly in fields like high-energy physics and telecommunications, demands precise and efficient examination tools. Our research introduces the ExamTIM library, designed to simplify the examination of time-stamped data and enable swift development of tailored observation methods. With a focus on event-driven approaches, ExamTIM consists of an adaptable framework that facilitates the creation of diverse observation techniques, such as: 
  time-merging and sorting operations, similar to those found in FlowCap2; 
  customized sampling procedures, analogous to those employed in SFARM; 
  enriched events, inspired by the principles of the EXODUS detector's data examination. 

In addition to its core functionality, the library encompasses time-axis management and data rendering tools, with data visualization capabilities, and a built-in CLI interface for effortless examination of data streams. Our proposed toolkit incorporates an efficient data representation system, taking into account the continuity and finite nature of the time axis, enabling seamless support of event-driven approaches and seamless examination of data streams.
